<title>UK: Close Brothers year pretax profit jumps.</title>
<headline>Close Brothers year pretax profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  24.8		 vs 22.2</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   10.0		 vs 8.5</p>
<p> Pretax			 45.11		vs 33.96</p>
<p> Operating income	   102.63	     vs 74.47</p>
<p> Bad/doubtful debt charge 4.13		 vs 3.03</p>
<p> Tax			    15.73		vs 11.79</p>
<p> Net taxed		    29.38		vs 22.16</p>
<p> Net interest income	50.19		vs 41.19</p>
<p> Admin expenses	     51.12		vs 35.65</p>
<p> Attributable		 28.67		vs 21.09</p>
<p>NOTE - UK investment banking group Close Brothers Group Plc said the year had been its 21st of unbroken increase in profits. Administrative expenses as a proportion of operating income were only 50 percent and the group was confident about the future.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
